jitArithOperandT -- SEQ 377 R1 (Tony): SEQ 376 R2 covers jitEmitBinary and unary negate -- a computed result never lands
on its operand's jitData. An inlined callee's every argument read follows to ONE node, the caller's operand (aoA, 7 at run
time; the build saw 3). Before the cure `argument - 1` left its sub on that node, so the next read of argument read 6, and
`-argument` left its neg there for the read after it. Intended: jitted = interpreted, 6/7/-7/7/7. aoX reads the binary's
RETURNED node (the assignment stores what the op hands back), so it witnesses the own-node half (SEQ 377 R2): return the
operand instead and aoX reads 7.
